 denuclearization of  the Korean Peninsula and the language is  important we don't know who does what we  don't know exactly what that means  because the document they signed says  literally just that the DPRK commits to  working towards complete  denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula  and the important language would be a  commitment towards complete verifiable  irreversible denuclearization right we  don't have that and asked more directly  whether Kim jong-un pledged to actually  get rid of his nukes Trump said we're  starting that process very quickly and  North Korea has done similar things  before several times and I've said many  times that the language of  denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula  can mean many different things for Kim  jong-un in the past for North Korean  leaders in the past it has meant  American forces leaving South Korea  altogether for the u.s. it has met North  Korea giving up every nuke that it has  South Korea has made it clear that North  Korea knows exactly what the United  States means by denuclearization but  they play coy with the language  deliberately so that is really the  majority of this thing and now Mike  Pompeo and the North Korean official are  going to be negotiating further I want  to be really clear here I was hoping for  success I was hoping for something  tangible there is no question that this  is a possible change in tone but the  real achievement of the summit is that  Kim jong-un got what he wanted which is  he met with an American president he was  treated like a normal real world leader  with reporting around the world about  this and Trump the great deal maker  the same vague commitments from North  Korea as prior presidents have received  but he gave Kim jong-un the photo-op and  he allowed Kim jong-un to get the  worldwide attention in exchange I  wouldn't have this guy help me negotiate  a car lease he got what everybody else  has gotten but he gave away a lot he  succeeded in legitimizing a dictator  without getting anything of new  practical value while giving a major  propaganda win to North Korea the the  piece of paper they signed is very  similar to the 1994 agreement will with  Bill Clinton it's similar to other  agreements but Kim jong-un in the end  got the photo-op that he wanted and the  big boy meeting with an American  president so the most notable element to  me here is once again not only the  suspension by the u.s. of the military  exercises but also that Trump is at  least theoretically agreeing to provide  some security guarantees in the future  and that would actually be a major  change and the prudence of which can be  debated the prudence of which is  questionable because if you were Donald  Trump and you say I'm willing to provide  security guarantees that is once again  the type of at least pseudo commitment  that doesn't actually put Kim jong-un in  a position of having to do anything  and Trump is trying to make this appear  as though it is a major victory Trump is  bizarrely gushing over Kim jong-un  saying after the fact that Kim jong-un  is smart and talented and a really funny  guy this is more praise than Donald  Trump has recently given the Canadian  Prime Minister Justin Trudeau who's  presumably our ally and Kim jong-un is a  brutal dictator but he is smart talented  and funny in the eyes of Donald Trump  will this be good for Trump that's  actually a really interesting question  regardless of the fact that nothing real  and tangible was achieved by this summit  it still could be good for Donald  Trump's reelection chances it might even  be good for Republicans in November  because many trumpets aren't going to  read past the headlines period they  signed a piece of paper there have been  months  of talking this up people talking about  a Nobel Peace Prize for Donald Trump and  we ended with a document whose value is  merely that they are going to have more  talks but Kim Jong un now has worldwide  headlines for weeks and the signal that  Donald Trump sent is if you acquire  nukes and you threaten the world and you  brutalize your own people you can earn  yourself a face-to-face with an American  president to worldwide acclaim you tell  me what signal that sense if you are  other countries that are starting to  think you know maybe Kim jong-un is on  to something maybe we should grab some  nukes from whoever will sell them to us  and see how that works for us  extraordinarily dangerous and I'm  genuinely I I don't relish this right I  actually wish I could come to you I mean  in my dream I was thrilled I had this  dream where Trump did it and I I was  actually saying I'm gonna have to go on  the show today and say this is a  historic and incredible achievement by  our president I wish I could come and  tell you that literally only in my  dreams did that actually take place the  video you just finished watching was  made possible by you through the  membership program you can sign up for  membership at david pakman.com slash  membership we are viewer supported  independent media you can use the coupon  code  I voted 17 for a 40% discount off of  your membership
 

